# Story 32: Batch Commands (##cmd) (45s)
# Hook: Run the same command across every pane in a scope at once.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-032-batch-commands.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Run the same command across every pane in a scope at once.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and create a few panes so the batch has something to fan out across.

[00:09.0 --> 00:20.0]
The cmd command takes a scope and a shell command. Cmd stack pwd runs pwd in every pane of the stack -- one line in, one line per pane out.

[00:20.0 --> 00:30.0]
Scopes range from a single pane up to the whole workspace: pane, pg, stack, lane, tab, and ws. Cmd lane echoes a build into every pane of the lane.

[00:30.0 --> 00:40.0]
Need to target somewhere you're not focused? Add selectors like --tab, --lane, --pg, or --pane to aim the batch precisely.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
One command, fanned out across your whole layout.

